# Codex Handoff

## Current Focus
- Import review reconciliation was simplified for parsed PDF statements.
- PDF transactions are only saved when statement math verifies against beginning and ending balances.
- If PDF transaction math cannot be verified or does not match, DebtScope saves the balance snapshot only.
- Structured transaction files remain the recommended path for transaction history.

## Files Changed
- `DebtScope/View/Import/ReviewImportView.swift`
- `DebtScope/View/Import/StatementCheckSheet.swift`

## ReviewImportView Notes
- `currentStatementCheckResult` computes PDF-only reconciliation review state.
- `statementCheckSnapshotOnlyMessage` shows the orange import-review row.
- The orange row is a single tappable line:
  `Balances only will be saved. Import CSV/QIF/etc for transactions. Tap to view reconciliation.`
- Tapping the orange row sets `statementCheckDetailsResult` and opens the reconciliation sheet.
- The reconciliation sheet uses item-based presentation instead of a boolean, preventing blank presentations.
- The reconciliation sheet now presents with `.large` only.
- `applyDefaultStatementCheckRulesIfNeeded(to:)` excludes all PDF transactions when reconciliation fails or cannot verify, then continues saving the snapshot.
- QFX/OFX/QBO/QIF/CSV/Excel/ZIP transaction imports are not blocked by this PDF rule.

## StatementCheckSheet Notes
- `StatementCheckSheet` supports `isReadOnly`.
- In read-only mode, action buttons are hidden.
- The title is `Statement totals do not match` for arithmetic mismatches.
- The mismatch message explains that DebtScope saved the snapshot only because transactions did not match statement balances.
- The unverifiable message explains that the statement lacked enough balance data to verify transactions.
- Both read-only messages include supported transaction import types:
  CSV, OFX/QFX/QBO, QIF, Excel (XLSX/XLS), or ZIP.
- Read-only mismatch details use the section title `Reconciliation Details`.

## Validation
- Xcode live diagnostics were clean for `ReviewImportView.swift` and `StatementCheckSheet.swift`.
- Full Xcode project build completed successfully after the changes.

## Follow-Up Checks
- Manually test a PDF with matching totals: green success row should appear and transactions should save.
- Manually test a PDF with mismatched totals: orange row should appear, reconciliation sheet should open full-size, and only snapshots should save.
- Manually test a structured file import: transactions should still save through the existing flow.
